{"id":"07984690152581ad","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-df-zfc-preserves-cardinal.md","title":"ZFC Preserves Cardinal","display":"df-zfc-preserves-cardinal — ZFC Preserves Cardinal","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-preserves-cardinal","aliases":["58-df-zfc-preserves-cardinal"],"display":"df-zfc-preserves-cardinal — ZFC Preserves Cardinal","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","[[../batch15/58-df-zfc-forcing2-forcing-poset.md]]","[[../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-preserves-cardinal"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-preserves-cardinal</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-preserves-cardinal — ZFC Preserves Cardinal"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b5833df5ef175153\" href=\"?note=b5833df5ef175153\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-zfc-forcing2-forcing-poset.md\">../batch15/58-df-zfc-forcing2-forcing-poset.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md\">../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"46b2495f214783c3\" href=\"?note=46b2495f214783c3\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md\">../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P})\">\\((\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P})\\)</span> (forcing preorder with greatest condition)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> (ground-model cardinal) and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\check\\kappa\">\\(\\check\\kappa\\)</span> (its canonical forcing name)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Card}}(v_0)\">\\(\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Card}}(v_0)\\)</span> (a fixed object-language formula code defining cardinality)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\\Vdash_{V,(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P})}\\varphi[\\vec\\tau]\">\\(p\\Vdash_{V,(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P})}\\varphi[\\vec\\tau]\\)</span> (the ambient-universe forcing-relation class schema, with the order and name tuple displayed)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PreservesCardinal}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{PreservesCardinal}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span> (metatheoretic predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcing2ForcingPoset}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcing2ForcingPoset}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\)</span> (predicates from the dependencies)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}preserves\\text{-}cardinal}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{PreservesCardinal}_S(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P},\\kappa)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcing2ForcingPoset}_S\n(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P})\n\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\n1_{\\mathbb P}\\Vdash_{V,(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P})}\n\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Card}}[\\langle\\check\\kappa\\rangle].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}preserves\\text{-}cardinal}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{PreservesCardinal}_S(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P},\\kappa)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcing2ForcingPoset}_S\n(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P})\n\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\n1_{\\mathbb P}\\Vdash_{V,(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P})}\n\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Card}}[\\langle\\check\\kappa\\rangle].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The forced assertion is a fixed object-language formula code together with its one-name tuple; the external predicate <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\)</span> is not inserted into object syntax.</li>\n<li>Ambient <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> is a proper class, so this use of the forcing theorem is explicitly metatheoretic. For a set-coded ground model, the six-place forcing relation from the dependency must be used instead.</li>\n<li>Since <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"1_{\\mathbb P}\">\\(1_{\\mathbb P}\\)</span> is greatest, forcing cardinality at <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"1_{\\mathbb P}\">\\(1_{\\mathbb P}\\)</span> is equivalent to forcing it at every condition.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-zfc-forcing2-forcing-poset.md","status":"resolved","id":"b5833df5ef175153","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-zfc-forcing2-forcing-poset.md]]","embed":false},{"targ